.TH GITRLZ 1 "2026-07-21" "gitrl-z 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitrlz \- visual git reflog browser with reset preview
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitrlz
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.RI [ PATH ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitrl-z
is a visual browser for the git reflog. It lists reflog entries the way
.BR gitg (1)
lists commits, and previews what a
.B git reset \-\-hard
would do before you run it.
.PP
The reflog remembers where every branch has been, including commits that a
rebase rewrote or a reset abandoned.
.B gitrlz
lists it, and when an entry is selected it draws the commit graph as it
would look if that entry's branch were reset there.
.PP
.B gitrlz
is read only. It never writes to the repository: no ref is moved, no working
tree is touched, no index is written. The preview is computed in memory, and
the command that would produce it is shown for you to run yourself.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B gitrlz
opens the repository containing the current working directory. Outside a
repository it opens a chooser listing recently used ones. Given a
.IR PATH ,
it opens the repository containing that path instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window rather than reusing an existing one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-wd
Do not open the working directory's repository. Used by the desktop entry.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal run.
.TP
.B 1
A
.I PATH
argument is not inside a git repository, or the display could not be opened.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F5
Reload the repository.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-reflog (1),
.BR git\-reset (1),
.BR gitg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
alexandros filotheou <alexandros.filotheou@gmail.com>
.PP
